# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this, Git's autocrlf setting rewrites line endings on checkout and
# every text file shows as modified on a fresh clone. That matters more here than
# usual: start.cmd and the other launchers are batch files that must keep the
# line endings cmd.exe expects, and a stray conversion is the sort of thing that
# only shows up on someone else's machine.

# Batch files MUST be CRLF, or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The PowerShell build and verification scripts are Windows-only too.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Source and documentation stay LF, which is what the tooling expects.
*.java  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf

# The Maven wrapper's properties file is read by the wrapper script.
mvnw.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.jar   binary
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary

# Exported archives and diffs.
*.pdf   binary
